PATCH 479: FUN_1000_9dd2, the AI SUPPORT-REQUEST handler -- the BX side index was bound to the
uninitialised pseudo-var `unaff_CS` and the request queue was walked as `int *` (stride 24) through a
host-deref'd near pointer.

asm 0x19dd2-0x19e4e (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00), reached from b0be with di=the requesting object: byte[di+0x16]
bit3 selects the side (bx=0/2 -> the busy word 0x9454/0x9456, the enable word 0x9450+bx, the last-request
stamp 0x9460+bx and the queue head 0x9458+bx); the request is rate-limited to one per 0x1e0 frames, calls
out via bf3c(3,bx,di), then walks the 16-entry, 0xc-byte-stride queue for a free slot to record the object
and the tick word[0x452] (a4a2(0x2f2a) + bee2(0x25,0xb4)), answering a4a2(0x2edd) + bee2(0x27,0xb4) when
the queue is full or the side is busy/disabled.  Rebuilt 1:1; the first AI support request of the AZER1
self-play SEGV'd here.
